  "notes": "ARC Prize page verified directly by the owner. The two ARC harnesses are DIFFERENT QUESTIONS and carry distinct comparability_group values so they cannot be cross-ranked. Standard is the striking result: max scores HIGHEST (62.71%) AND costs LEAST ($26,098) — ARC attributes this to higher effort taking fewer actions, hence fewer model calls. That is a direct counterexample to treating reasoning effort as a cost multiplier, and it contradicts the plateau shape seen on the coding benchmarks. Under the Provider Adapter every effort is near saturation (~98-100%), so that harness cannot discriminate efforts at all.",
  "claims": [],
  "missing": [
    "Per-task cost under either ARC harness — only total suite cost is published",
    "Whether the Standard-harness cost inversion generalizes beyond ARC-AGI-3's interactive-game structure"
  ],
